{"seq":18,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T07:13:49.111Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"7a398ca47ccabf961ac48f12b73678580684625a90f53a89937ad099cdcf1d62","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Tobias, I found three ticket numbers that look like Marrow Fieldworks, but none of them is tied to the account by name. Here's each one with its source:\n\n**From Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" digest** (teams/team-central/digests, 2 Jan 2026)\n- **#4409**: a timeout that kept coming back on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard. It hit Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake.\n- **#4412**: a minor glitch in the driver SMS prompt when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n\nThe digest says Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on Mon 5 Jan. It lists both tickets as open items Hollis flagged on \"Pree's dealer account\" before that handoff. I'm reading that as Marrow Fieldworks from the context, but the digest doesn't say so outright. I also can't see whether either ticket was closed after January.\n\n**From #central-random** (your message, 13 Oct, 09:27)\n- **#8841**: West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots still double-books when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. Hollis had asked about the tractor-bay alerts on \"Tobias's dealer account.\" I'm assuming that's Marrow Fieldworks, but the channel never names it.\n\n**What I left out:**\n- **FR-882**, in the same Moss digest. It's a feature request from **Marrow Agrisupply**, a different account. It asks for custom pallet-jack icons on the yard map, and support sent it to the product backlog.\n- Moss's Central cheat sheet has a \"door 4 msg\" note under Marrow Agrisupply, but no ticket number.\n- I looked through Moss's other public notes. They're all North team accounts and